# M3 gate review — legacy Python compiler retirement (`3dd59171`)

The core removal is sound and the ANTLR frontend is correctly installed as the only Python frontend. I am not granting sign-off because two user-facing documentation surfaces still assert the retired frontend exists, and one is in a file this commit edited.

## 1. Completeness of the removal — PASS (with one untracked-by-the-grep leftover)

- Deleted as reported: `src/cljc/yang/python.cljc`, `test/yang/python_test.clj`, `src/cljc/yang/docs/python.md`.
- An exact-boundary grep of `src/` and `test/` finds no require or reference to the removed namespace. Remaining matches are all legitimate: `yang.python.antlr*`, test ids (`:yang.python/cst`, `:yang.python/antlr`, `:yang.python/uninstalled`), and the `yang.python` test-subsystem prefix in `src/dev/subsystems.edn:50` (intentional, it covers `yang.python.antlr`).
- No `:yang.python/legacy` registration or id remains in code or tests. The only occurrences are the historical amendment prose in `docs/design/yang.antlr.md:3077,3080`.
- Catalog verified in `src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:62-75`: `:yang.clojure/legacy` (default, `:clojure`), `:yang.php/legacy` (`:php`), `:yang.python/antlr` (`:python`, revision `f4`, targets `#{:java :javascript :dart}`). `antlr-manifest` changed `:python.antlr` → `:python`; nothing else matches on `:python.antlr`.
- Kondo independently reproduced: whole-repo `29 errors, 71 warnings`; the changed Clojure files lint `0 errors, 0 warnings`. I spot-checked three errors (`src/cljd/dao/postgraphics/flutter.cljd:406`, `src/cljd/dao/stream/cbor/cljd.cljd:193`, `test/dao/stream/waitset/driver_test.cljd:72`) and the ANTLR-adjacent `src/cljd/yang/antlr/cst.cljd:55,58`; every one is in a file whose diff against `79db800e` is empty. None is introduced by this commit.
- Caveat: `demo_python.clj:3` (tracked, repo root) still has `(require '[yang.python :as py])`, so the report's "Nothing else requires `yang.python`" is false outside the `src`/`test` scope it cites. See P3-1.

## 2. Deliberate capability loss — scoping is correct; docs record it only in the commit/report

The scoping is right and implemented, not merely asserted:

- Module globals are a dict; reads go through `py/global-get` (`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:489-496`), and a miss in both the module dict and builtins raises `NameError` (`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:825-835`).
- Tests pin the behavior: `test/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc:216,234` (`NameError: name 'x' is not defined`) and `test/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc:1592-1610`.
- The regression is stated plainly in the commit message and `collab/m3-report.log`, and §8.10 says cross-language calls need an ABI.

Gap: no design or user doc says "legacy Python could call Clojure macros/functions in the same session; the ANTLR frontend cannot until §8.10". The §8.5.6 amendment is the natural place for that sentence. The removed Python branch in `repl_test.cljc` was the executable record of the capability; it was deleted rather than converted into a NameError assertion (generic NameError is covered, a Clojure-defined-name case is not). P3, not a scoping error.

## 3. `(compile ...)` defect not masked — PASS

The only changes on this path are test relocations: `test/yin/repl_test.cljc:185-189` and `test/yin/repl/frontend_catalog_test.cljc:68` now select PHP and compile `1 + 2;`. No source change touches `compile-source`, `compile-command-ast`, `render-compile-output`, or the frontend binding. Nothing fakes or swallows the ANTLR path; the failure is disclosed as open item 1. The consequence is a disclosed coverage gap: the ANTLR `(compile ...)` path is now untested (and known broken on Node / very slow on the JVM).

## 4. Docs accuracy — REQUEST CHANGES

**P2-1 — `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:85-87` still says the deleted frontend exists.** In the same "Using Python at the prompt" section that was just rewritten, the document still reads:

> "The legacy Python frontend has no parser dependency and runs on every host, but it is the old hand-written frontend, not the ANTLR pipeline."

This directly contradicts the retirement stated at lines 49-55. The surrounding prerequisite note is also JVM-only even though the ANTLR frontend now claims every host. Fix: delete the legacy sentence and state the all-host generation prerequisite (`bb gen:antlr` / the per-target artifacts), or mark the old behavior explicitly historical.

**P2-2 — `public/chp/yang.chp` is live, linked from the global template, and still markets the deleted compiler.** `world.server` serves `public/`, and `/yang.chp` is linked from `template.chp:44`, `faq.chp:18`, and `yin.chp:15`. The page still has:
- the `yang.python` compiler with a "complete tokenizer and recursive-descent parser" (`:64-98`), including the tokenizer/AST tables;
- a `(yang.python/compile "lambda x: x * 3")` sample (`:117-119`);
- "Python Compiler Source — 450+ lines including tokenizer and parser" (`:194-196`);
- the now-false claim "Python functions can call Clojure functions and vice versa" (`:30`) and "seamless cross-language function calls" (`:167` region), which the deliberate capability loss contradicts until §8.10.

This is the most user-visible stale surface. Rewrite the Python section to the ANTLR frontend and remove/qualify the bidirectional-interop claim.

**Named items in the brief:**
- `docs/cross-language-macro.md`: acceptable as left — its header (lines 1-6) already declares it historical and says its expander target is deleted. Optional: add that its `yang.python` target is also deleted.
- `assignments.md:428` and `assignment_strategies.md:152`: the "In `yang/python.cljc`" samples are stale and present-tense ("Update Python Compiler"). They do mislead slightly; mark historical or strip the implementation instructions. P3.
- `yang.antlr.md` §8.5.6 amendment and §1 note: accurate. The docstring fix in `yang.python.antlr.repl` is accurate.
- The catalog section of `yin.repl.md` is accurate apart from P2-1.

**Other stale references found (P3):** `docs/design/yang.antlr.md:3998` (Phase 1 exit criterion still says the legacy frontend remains selectable until the gate; amend to past tense/satisfied), `:3190` (F3 row says "(JVM)", superseded by the 2026-10-17 amendment at 3224), `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:335` (cites deleted `src/cljc/yang/python.cljc:481`), `docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:815` (`yang.python` should be `yang.python.antlr`), `docs/design/yang.typescript.md:1522` ("pulls from `yang.python`", though the listed namespaces are `yang.python.antlr.*`). Also `test/yin/repl_test.cljc:719`: the test name still says "other languages" but now covers PHP only.

